Subject: [PATCH] Request the permissions the default SMS app needs on Android
 17

Android recognises the default SMS app (Telephony.Sms.getDefaultSmsPackage,
SmsApplication) only when the app ops in DEFAULT_APP_EXCLUSIVE_APPOPS are
allowed for it, among them RECEIVE_WAP_PUSH and READ_CELL_BROADCASTS. These
app ops follow runtime permissions, and the SMS role grants a permission
only when the app requests it. Messaging did not request these two, so on
Android 17 the app ops stayed "ignore": the app held the SMS role but kept
asking to become the default SMS app, could not send and posted no
notification for received messages (LECH OS on the Pixel 9, 7. 11. 2026).
The Messaging app of GrapheneOS requests both.
---
 AndroidManifest.xml | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/AndroidManifest.xml b/AndroidManifest.xml
--- a/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -30,2 +30,6 @@
     <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.SEND_SMS"/>
+    <!-- LECH OS: the default SMS app needs these app ops (SmsApplication); the SMS role grants the
+         permissions behind them only when they are requested. -->
+    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.RECEIVE_WAP_PUSH"/>
+    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.READ_CELL_BROADCASTS"/>
     <!-- Application needs access to MMS network -->
